{
  "slug": "artist:tyree",
  "name": "Tyree Cooper",
  "editorial_article": "Chicago-born producer Tyree Cooper launched his career in 1986 with the track \"I Fear the Night\" on DJ International Records, helping establish the foundational house music sound of his home city. A pioneer of the hip house subgenre, he rose to international recognition when his 1988 track \"Turn Up the Bass,\" featuring rapper Kool Rock Steady, reached number 12 on the UK Singles Chart. His 1987 release \"Acid Over\" remains a core artifact of the classic acid house era. Beyond his early club successes, Cooper has remained a fixture of the global scene, collaborating with artists including Fast Eddie, Marc Romboy, and Sebastian Krieg across labels such as Dance Mania, Ovum Recordings, and Frisbee Tracks.",
